# Review routing for the files a quality gate derives its verdict from.
#
# GitHub only *requests* the review here. It becomes merge-blocking only when
# the `main-protection` ruleset sets `require_code_owner_review: true`, which
# it deliberately does not (solo project, `required_approving_review_count:
# 0` -- see docs/development/repo-governance.md). So this is a "a human should
# look at this diff" list, not access control, and GitHub never counts the PR
# author's own approval toward a required code-owner review -- which is why
# the ruleset switch is deferred until there is a second maintainer.
#
# Scope: the gates a PR can otherwise move by regenerating the artifact
# itself -- committed baselines, generated contracts, schema dumps -- plus
# the registry/config that defines what blocks a merge. Not exhaustive and
# not a security boundary. Add a path when you add a gate whose number or
# allowlist is itself the enforcement.
#
# Rationale and the "adding a quality gate" procedure: .github/AGENTS.md.

